Data
----
The data the project makes itself is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (the file LICENSE-DATA). That is:

  - registry/*.csv, except registry/catalogue.csv (see below)
  - evidence/*.csv
  - the files the project's own jobs publish, such as orbit_gap.json and
    fitted_orbits.json on the orbit-checks branch

Credit it as "data from OpenGNSS (opengnss.org)".

Data from others
----------------
These keep their owners' terms. Neither licence above applies to them.

  - data/*.json and latest_gnss.json on the orbit-data branch: orbital
    records from Space-Track.org and CelesTrak, under their terms of use.
  - registry/catalogue.csv: from the General Catalog of Artificial Space
    Objects (GCAT) by Jonathan McDowell, under CC BY. Cite it as
    "data from GCAT (J. McDowell, planet4589.org/space/gcat)".
    registry/library_counts.csv and registry/library_matching.csv are
    counted from GCAT, so they carry the same credit as well as ours.
  - registry/satellites.csv and registry/signal_ids.csv are built from the
    International GNSS Service (IGS) satellite metadata file, and IGS
    broadcast navigation files are read from BKG. Acknowledge the IGS when
    using them.
  - ui/figures/land.json: Natural Earth 110 m land, public domain (CC0).
  - latest_news.json on the news-data branch: headlines and excerpts belong
    to the publishers they came from.
